# Runbooks

Every alert in `kubernetes/flux/prometheusrule.yaml`{% if database == 'postgres' and secrets_backend == 'onepassword' %} and
`kubernetes/db/prometheusrule.yaml`{% endif %} links its section here through its
`runbook_url`. Platform alerts, and the platform side of the causes below, live
in the [cluster runbooks]({{ runbook_url }}). Every command here only reads. A
fix ships as a {{ change_request }}, never a `kubectl apply`.

## AppDown

Deployment `{{ app_slug }}` has had no available replica for 10m.

```bash
kubectl -n {{ app_namespace }} get deploy {{ app_slug }}
kubectl -n {{ app_namespace }} describe deploy {{ app_slug }}
kubectl -n {{ app_namespace }} get events --sort-by=.lastTimestamp
kubectl -n {{ app_namespace }} logs deploy/{{ app_slug }}
```

A crash loop or a failing readiness probe is the app.
{%- if secrets_backend != 'none' %}
`CreateContainerConfigError` means the Secret has not synced, so check
`kubectl -n {{ app_namespace }} get externalsecret`.
{%- endif %}
`ImagePullBackOff` means the image reference or the pull credential, so check
`image:` in kubernetes/flux/deployment.yaml
{%- if secrets_backend != 'none' and enable_registry_pull_secret %} and
`kubectl -n {{ app_namespace }} get externalsecret {{ app_slug }}-registry`
{%- endif %}.
`Pending` is a platform problem: [cluster runbooks]({{ runbook_url }}).

## AppAbsent

Prometheus has had no kube-state-metrics series for Deployment `{{ app_slug }}`
for 15m, so the Deployment is gone or nothing reports it.

```bash
kubectl -n {{ app_namespace }} get deploy
flux get kustomizations -n flux-system {{ app_slug }}
```

A missing Deployment means Flux pruned it or never applied it, so fix the
Kustomization. When the Deployment exists, kube-state-metrics or Prometheus is
down, which is a platform problem: [cluster runbooks]({{ runbook_url }}).
{%- if database == 'postgres' and secrets_backend == 'onepassword' %}

## DatabaseAbsent

No instance of the `{{ app_slug }}-db` CloudNativePG cluster has had its
exporter scraped for 15m. The database is down, its pod is unschedulable, or
the PodMonitor or the scrape policy is broken.

```bash
kubectl -n {{ app_namespace }} get cluster {{ app_slug }}-db
kubectl -n {{ app_namespace }} get pods -l cnpg.io/cluster={{ app_slug }}-db
flux get kustomizations -n flux-system {{ app_slug }}-db
```

A running instance with no scrape points at `kubernetes/db/podmonitor.yaml` or
`kubernetes/db/networkpolicy.yaml`. A stopped or unschedulable instance is the
[cluster's CloudNativePG runbook]({{ db_runbook_url }}).
{%- endif %}
